From c9c2940dc84561a58fc997073daf550dd66993d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:23:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Validate external snapshots and report engine-correction
 impact

contract-compare now refuses a snapshot that is not a valid bundle and
names every structural problem; contract-validate runs the same check on
its own, and docs/contract-bundle.schema.json publishes the format. A
producer without field definitions may list plain keys and declare
absent records missing; absent definitions are reported, not diffed.
engine-impact compares two snapshots of the same imports and reports
rows removed, added or changed per metric and every company's score
before and after; its corrections can be attached to an export so a
conflict on a corrected key is flagged, not hidden. Exports now carry
observations for profile, price, ownership, corporate-action and
disclosure keys as well as data points.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
